    {
      "topic": "Actual source theorem and point",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "FrameWith26-72 contains precisely the even span, nontrivial twist, conjugate-dual polarization, independent odd kappa classes and mixed paired trace hypotheses. Its subgroup contains all commutators and is therefore normal; no stronger property is used by the new proof. Group-valued representations and characters are automatically invertible. MapSpan14-83 and DetAsm165-213 transport the original characteristic-prime point to these data, over FractionRing k[[t]]=k((t)); characteristic zero is not assumed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Group-algebra derivations and one-entry propagation",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "For R=F[H], the maps D_z(h)=z(h)rho(h) satisfy the exact derivation law because both twists restrict trivially to H. On I=ker(pi), D(p x q)=pi(p)D(x)pi(q). Surjectivity onto the full even algebra supplies both matrix-unit lifts, so a single killed entry forces the entire indicated off-diagonal block to vanish on I."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Central block idempotent and sign",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "For the row-block identity e and a corner-valued derivation delta, the identity eX=Xe yields delta(X)=X delta(e)-delta(e)X. Thus the primitive is +delta(e) for the convention dY(g)=A_gY-Y. This argument works over the actual positive-characteristic field and requires no general theorem about derivations of semisimple algebras."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Separation of the two twists",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Independently expanded A_(c^-1)z(chc^-1)=tau(c)z(h)-d_1(A_(c^-1)z(c))(h). Subtracting the original relation gives the displayed P_L with denominator chi(c)-1 and the stated plus signs. The denominator is nonzero by the retained source condition."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Extension from H and polarization",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "After subtracting the projected coboundary, comparison on hg=g(g^-1hg) makes every remaining value invariant under H. Full even span then forces the corner value to vanish. The conjugate-dual representation identity gives (d_tau P(sigma g))^T=d_tau(P^T)(g). Hence P+epsilon P^T restores both blocks with exactly the required sign; no assumption sigma(H)=H or division by two is added."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Paired product and four-factor trace",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The exact order lambda*kappa cancels the reversed term in the commutator and yields Q(xy)=Q(x)pi(y)+pi(x)Q(y)+sum(D_i(x)T_i(y)+T_i(x)D_i(y)). For x,y in I, applying trace to x p_v y p_u kills the Q terms and selects precisely D_i(x)_(uv)T_i(y)_(vu)+T_i(x)_(uv)D_i(y)_(vu). The trace relation is essential and preserved."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Conclusion and edge cases",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Fixing y makes the extracted relation a one-entry kernel relation. The first part forces every coefficient T_i(y)_(vu)=0; applying it in the opposite block to one lambda proves its polarized coboundary. The zero lower block gives O=0 and the empty cocycle family is vacuous. These are exactly the OddPart conclusions, with no hidden even-correction or finite auxiliary-choice conclusion."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Reproducible checks and scope",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Independently reran the offline checker: all ten source blobs, the exact free-associative paired identity with three negative controls, 4890 matrix-unit trace cases, and 24 finite-field corner-derivation cases passed. General derivations, twist separation and point transport were checked mathematically. No Lean compilation, entire Selmer bound or whole proof-node completion is asserted."
    }
